.TH BREWMASTER.PY 1 "2026-09-12" "3.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
brewmaster.py \- a graphical, fast, careful Homebrew upgrader
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python3 brewmaster.py
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B brewmaster.py
is an enhanced Homebrew upgrade wrapper. It renders outdated packages as a
box\-drawn table with version diffs, pipelines parallel downloads against
sequential installs, retries failed packages individually with timeouts and
backoff, skips pinned packages, supports interactive per\-package selection,
refuses to run twice at once, and audits every subprocess to
.I ~/.brewmaster.log\c
\&.
.PP
Running without flags performs an interactive upgrade: it updates Homebrew
metadata (skipped automatically if updated within the last hour), lists all
outdated packages with version diffs, prompts for confirmation, then upgrades
each package individually behind a live progress bar while the next packages
download in the background — retrying failures before reporting a summary.
.PP
Column arithmetic is done in terminal columns rather than characters: emoji and
CJK text are double\-width, while combining marks, variation selectors and
joiners take no space at all. Borders line up whatever a package name contains,
and truncation never splits a double\-width character in half.
.PP
All presentation degrades on its own. A non\-TTY output stream, the
.B NO_COLOR
environment variable,
.B TERM=dumb
or a non\-UTF\-8 stream independently drop color, the live progress line, or
box\-drawing characters; the content is never lost.
.PP
The
.B brew
executable is resolved once to an absolute path; a warning is printed if it
lives outside the standard Homebrew locations.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Selection
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Auto-approve all upgrades without an interactive prompt.
Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-interactive .
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interactive
Show a numbered table and choose which packages to upgrade. Accepts
selections like
.BR 1,3,5\-7 ,
.BR all ,
or
.BR none .
Selection implies consent; no second confirmation prompt is shown.
.TP
.BI \-\-skip " PKG " [ PKG " ...]"
Space-separated list of package names to exclude. Glob patterns are
supported via fnmatch:
.RS
.EX
python3 brewmaster.py --skip node 'python@*'
.EE
.RE
.TP
.BI \-\-only " PKG " [ PKG " ...]"
Upgrade only packages matching these names or globs. Everything else is
reported as skipped.
.B \-\-skip
wins where the two overlap.
.TP
.B \-\-formula\-only
Upgrade formulae only; skip all casks.
Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-cask\-only .
.TP
.B \-\-cask\-only
Upgrade casks only; skip all formulae.
Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-formula\-only .
.TP
.BR \-\-greedy " (default)"
Include auto-updating casks when checking for outdated packages.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-greedy
Disable greedy cask checking.
.SS Behaviour
.TP
.B \-\-check\-only
Report outdated packages with version diffs and exit without upgrading.
Exits with status 3 if any outdated packages were found.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print every command that would be executed without running any of them.
Skips the confirmation prompt and the instance lock.
.TP
.B \-\-backup
Before upgrading, dump the current Homebrew state to a timestamped Brewfile at
.IR ~/.brewmaster_backup_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.Brewfile
(mode 0600). The five newest backups are kept; older ones are pruned. A failed
dump prints a warning and writes nothing.
Restore with:
.RS
.EX
brew bundle install --file=~/.brewmaster_backup_<timestamp>.Brewfile
.EE
.RE
.TP
.B \-\-no\-update
Skip
.B brew update
entirely.
.TP
.B \-\-force\-update
Run
.B brew update
even if it already ran within the last hour. By default the update step is
skipped when the Homebrew repository's FETCH_HEAD is less than an hour old.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cleanup
Skip the
.B brew cleanup
step at the end of the run. Note that per-install cleanup is disabled during
the run, so nothing is reclaimed at all.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-lock
Allow concurrent runs by skipping the single-instance lock.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-config
Ignore
.IR ~/.brewmasterrc.json .
.TP
.B \-\-notify
Send a native macOS notification (via
.BR osascript )
when the run completes. Notification text is escaped to prevent AppleScript
injection.
.SS Performance
.TP
.BI \-\-jobs " N"
Number of parallel download workers, 1 to 16. Default is
.BR 6 .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-prefetch
Do not pre-download at all; let each
.B brew upgrade
fetch its own files.
.TP
.B \-\-sizes
Download everything up front and display per-package and total download sizes
in the table before the confirmation prompt. Note: this downloads before you
confirm.
.TP
.BI \-\-retries " N"
Number of attempts per package before it is marked failed. Retries use
exponential backoff. Default is
.BR 2 ,
minimum is
.BR 1 .
Errors that cannot succeed on a retry are never retried.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SECS"
Timeout per package upgrade in seconds. Default is
.BR 600 .
A hung installer becomes a recorded failure instead of stalling the run.
.SS Output
.TP
.BI \-\-color " auto|always|never"
Force or suppress ANSI color. Default
.B auto
respects
.BR NO_COLOR ,
.BR TERM=dumb ,
and whether stdout is a terminal.
.TP
.B \-\-ascii
ASCII-only output: no box-drawing characters and no emoji.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Print only warnings and errors. Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-interactive .
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Stream raw brew output instead of progress indicators.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print a machine-readable JSON summary of the run to stdout; all human-readable
output moves to stderr so the two never mix.
.TP
.B \-\-log\-json
Append one structured JSON record per run (upgraded packages, failures,
skipped count, elapsed time, bytes downloaded, space freed, exit code) to
.IR ~/.brewmaster_history.jsonl .
The file is trimmed to the newest 500 records.
.TP
.BI \-\-history " [N]"
Print the last N recorded runs as a table and exit. Default is
.BR 15 .
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success — nothing to do, or all upgrades succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
Fatal error (brew not found, unreadable
.BR "brew outdated" ,
non-interactive session without \-y, another run holds the lock, insufficient
disk space).
.TP
.B 2
Run completed but one or more packages failed.
.TP
.B 3
.B \-\-check\-only
found outdated packages.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted with Ctrl-C or SIGTERM.
.SH FEATURES
.SS Pipelined Parallel Downloads
Downloads run on a thread pool while upgrades install, not merely before them.
Fetches are submitted in upgrade order and the upgrade loop waits only on the
future for the package it is about to install, so the download of package N+1
overlaps the installation of package N.
.SS Faster brew Calls
Every brew subprocess runs with
.B HOMEBREW_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=1
and
.BR HOMEBREW_NO_INSTALL_CLEANUP=1 .
BrewMaster updates and cleans up once per run instead of letting Homebrew
re-check and re-clean on every package.
.B brew outdated
and
.B brew list --pinned
are issued concurrently.
.SS Smart Update Skipping
.B brew update
is skipped automatically when it ran within the last hour, saving the
slowest step of most runs.
.SS Single-Instance Lock
An flock on
.I ~/.brewmaster.lock
refuses to start a second run while one is in progress, so overlapping cron
jobs do not fight over Homebrew's own locks.
.SS Graceful Degradation
A failed
.B brew update
warns and continues against cached metadata; a failed
.B brew cleanup
warns after the upgrades have already succeeded; a failed prefetch is advisory
because the upgrade will fetch the file itself. Only genuinely unrecoverable
conditions exit 1.
.SS Disk Space Check
Free space on the Homebrew prefix is checked before upgrading. A run that
cannot fit its queued downloads is refused; a tight one warns and proceeds.
.SS Security Hardening
Package names are validated against brew's naming alphabet before reaching any
subprocess. Log, history, lock and backup files are created mode 0600, and the
log rotates at 2 MB keeping 3 generations. Subprocesses inherit no stdin, so a
cask demanding an interactive password fails fast instead of hanging. Every
subprocess call writes an AUDIT line with the exact shell-quoted command, exit
code, and duration to the log.
.SS Pin Awareness
Reads
.B brew list --pinned
and automatically skips pinned formulae. If the pinned-package query fails, a
warning is printed and the run continues.
.SS Clean Interrupts and Cron Safety
Ctrl-C or SIGTERM mid-upgrade prints how many packages were upgraded, failed,
and not attempted, cancels pending downloads, then exits 130. In a non-TTY
session without
.BR \-y ,
the tool exits 1 immediately instead of hanging on the prompt.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.I ~/.brewmasterrc.json
supplies defaults for any of
.BR skip ", " only ", " greedy ", " notify ", " backup ", " jobs ", " retries ,
.BR timeout ", " log_json ", " no_cleanup ", " no_prefetch ", " color ", and " ascii .
Command-line flags override it; unknown or mistyped keys warn and are ignored.
.PP
.EX
{
  "skip": ["python@*", "node"],
  "jobs": 8,
  "log_json": true
}
.EE
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Interactive upgrade (default):
.EX
python3 brewmaster.py
.EE
.TP
Pick packages from a numbered table:
.EX
python3 brewmaster.py -i
.EE
.TP
Auto-approve, skip node and all python versions, notify:
.EX
python3 brewmaster.py -y --skip node 'python@*' --notify
.EE
.TP
Upgrade only the Rust toolchain packages:
.EX
python3 brewmaster.py --only 'rust*' -y
.EE
.TP
Preview outdated packages (exit 3 if any found):
.EX
python3 brewmaster.py --check-only
.EE
.TP
Show per-package download sizes before confirming:
.EX
python3 brewmaster.py --sizes
.EE
.TP
Backup bundle, then upgrade formulae only:
.EX
python3 brewmaster.py --backup --formula-only
.EE
.TP
Cron-friendly run with JSON history:
.EX
python3 brewmaster.py -y -q --log-json
.EE
.TP
Feed the result to another tool:
.EX
python3 brewmaster.py -y --json | jq '.failures'
.EE
.TP
Review the last 30 recorded runs:
.EX
python3 brewmaster.py --history 30
.EE
.TP
Give a slow cask 20 minutes before treating it as hung:
.EX
python3 brewmaster.py --cask-only --timeout 1200 -y
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.brewmaster.log
Timestamped log of all runs with per-command AUDIT lines. Mode 0600, rotated
at 2 MB with 3 generations kept.
.TP
.I ~/.brewmaster_history.jsonl
One JSON record per run when
.B \-\-log\-json
is set, trimmed to the newest 500. Mode 0600.
.TP
.I ~/.brewmaster.lock
Single-instance lock held for the duration of a run. Mode 0600.
.TP
.I ~/.brewmasterrc.json
Optional defaults for command-line flags.
.TP
.I ~/.brewmaster_backup_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.Brewfile
Bundle snapshots created by
.BR \-\-backup ;
the five newest are kept. Mode 0600.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set, disables color under
.BR "\-\-color auto" .
.TP
.B TERM
.B dumb
or unset disables color and the live progress line under
.BR "\-\-color auto" .
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Python 3.10 or later (standard library only), Homebrew (
.I https://brew.sh
), macOS.
.PP
The
.B \-\-notify
flag requires
.B osascript
(available by default on macOS).
.PP
The
.B \-\-backup
flag requires the
.B brew-bundle
tap (included with Homebrew by default).
.SH AUTHOR
Anirban Bagchi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR brew (1)
